>1999</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>433</fpage><lpage>447</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10582782</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/humupd/5.5.433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lyytikainen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaasila</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Koskela</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Chlamydia trachomatis seroprevalence atlas of Finland 1983&#x02013;2003</article-title><source>Sex Transm Infect</source><year>2008</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17911135</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/sti.2007.027409</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Moji</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kusano</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurokawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawagoe</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Katamine</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trend in Chlamydia trachomatis infection among pregnant women in the past ten years in Japan: significance of Chlamydia trachomatis seroprevalence</article-title><source>Sex Transm Dis</source><year>1998</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>516</fpage><lpage>521</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9858346</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00007435-199811000-00004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hiltunen-Back</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Haikala</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Kautiainen</sur